            <div xml:id="d954">

                <pb facs="0969" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1A/108: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-04T19:00:00-05:00">October 4, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>408. Your 627, October 2, 2 p.m. If the present meeting of the Provisional
                    Council established under the Protocol of May 6 is converted <pb facs="0970"
                        n="958" xml:id="pg958"/> into a meeting of the permanent council to be
                    established under the International Sugar Agreement, you may continue to attend
                    and to participate in the proceedings but without power to vote formally. Your
                    appointments are specifically to the Provisional Council. Appointments to the
                    permanent council would have to be approved by the President. The United States
                    cannot assume the obligations of the Sugar Agreement or take formal action under
                    it, such as by full participation in the Council which it establishes, until the
                    Agreement has been ratified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
